## Safety Rules

These rules are non-negotiable. See [AI-Assisted Development Standards](https://github.com/planetary/.github/blob/main/standards/ai-assisted-development.md) for full context.

### Destructive Git Commands Are Forbidden

The following commands must never be run without explicit developer permission:

- `git checkout --` on any file
- `git restore` on any file
- `git reset` in any form
- `git clean`
- `git stash drop`
- `git push --force`

Do not revert uncommitted changes for any reason. If the build fails, if there are merge conflicts, or if changes seem problematic, **report the issue and ask the developer how to proceed**.

### Honesty About Untested Code

- Never claim code works if it has not been executed.
- Never imply code is "ready" or "complete" without verification.
- State explicitly: "I have not tested this yet."
- Warn about assumptions: "This assumes [X] exists."
- If tests were written but not run, say so clearly.

### No Unauthorized Actions

- Never push code to remote repositories without explicit permission.
- Never create, close, or comment on PRs or issues without permission.
- Never add AI attribution to commit messages, PR descriptions, or code comments.
- Never delete files without moving them to a safe location first and getting approval.

